    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Regularized compression coefficient of the Cahn-Hilliard moving-mesh forcing. The raw coefficient phi / (1 - gamma^2 phi^2) is singular as gamma*phi -&gt; 1, so phi is saturated through a tanh before being used. Both the value and its derivative w.r.t. the phase are returned (the derivative is used to linearize the forcing). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
